# Code launched over data it was given is separated from that data too (R22, item 1; plan M11 5b): a record there whose
# head is an ordinary Structure of the data launches it -- `Step(Inner)` and `Step(data := Inner)` run Step over Inner,
# `Twice()` runs Twice over itself.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call
# main(). The Structures inside D are written in one line each: a block closed by `end:` inside the parentheses of the
# part data is a later step of 5b.
sub: main () (
    Code:
        Step(Inner)
        Step(data := Inner)
        Twice()
    D:
        Inner: (int: x 1)
        Step: (x := x + 10)
        Twice: (int: k 0; k := k + 2)
)
    call: D Code
main()
int: seen main\data\D\Inner\x
int: twice main\data\D\Twice\k
